      "transcriber_notes": [
        "ROW ALIGNMENT CAUTION: in the print the stub (province names) column is set with slightly tighter line spacing than the figures, so names and figure lines drift out of register (at the top each name sits about half a line above its figures; near the bottom e.g. 'Yunnan' sits level with the line beginning 3.0 and 'Suiyuan' level with 98.6). There are 18 names and 18 figure lines, so figures were assigned to provinces strictly in printed order (line 1 = Chekiang ... line 18 = Chungking). Under this assignment every row sums to 100.0. If instead the visual level were followed, the first figure line would belong to Anhwei and the last line (14.0 / 0.1 / 85.9) would have no name; this alternative cannot be excluded, and rows Kwangsi–Chungking in particular should be treated with caution.",
        "Row sums (should be 100): Chekiang 100.0; Anhwei 100.0; Kiangsi 100.0; Hupeh 100.0; Hunan 100.0; Szechwan 100.0; Sikang 100.0; Honan 100.0; Shensi 100.0; Kansu 100.0; Fukien 100.0; Kwangtung 100.0; Kwangsi 100.0; Yunnan 100.0; Kweichow 100.0; Ningsia 100.0; Suiyuan 100.0; Chungking 100.0; Total 99.8",
        "The Total row gives overall percentages, not sums of the column; it adds across to 99.8 (printed components 82.9+0.6+6.6+5.2+1.9+2.2+0.3+0.1).",
        "Blank cells are blank in the print."
      ],
